<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.cometgui</groupId>
    <artifactId>cometgui-parent</artifactId>
    <version>0.1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
  </parent>

  <artifactId>cometgui-process</artifactId>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>
  <name>CometGUI :: Process service</name>
  <description>The only place in the product allowed to construct a ProcessBuilder (R-PROC-02).</description>

  <!--
    Only the edges the specification's layering permits are declared here.
    Adding one is an architectural change: say so in the phase handoff, and
    expect the ArchUnit rules in cometgui-archtests to have an opinion.
  -->
  <dependencies>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.cometgui</groupId>
      <artifactId>cometgui-domain</artifactId>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <plugins>
      <!--
        WHY THIS MODULE'S TESTS FORCE A UTF-8 LOCALE ON THE FORKED JVM.

        PHASE-03 exit gate item 4 is "paths containing spaces and non-ASCII
        characters work on the reference platform".  This build container has no
        UTF-8 locale selected: `locale -a` offers C, C.utf8 and POSIX, and
        neither LANG nor LC_ALL is set, so a JVM started here reports
        sun.jnu.encoding=ANSI_X3.4-1968 and native.encoding=ANSI_X3.4-1968.

        In that state the JVM cannot represent a non-ASCII file name AT
        ALL: Path.of("café") throws InvalidPathException before any product code
        runs.  The gate item would be untestable, and an untestable gate item has
        not passed.

        The system property sun.jnu.encoding does NOT fix it: the JVM derives that property
        from the OS locale during startup, before system properties are applied.
        The environment variable does, and it is the same thing a real desktop
        user's session already has.  So the forked test JVM is given one.

        This is a TEST ENVIRONMENT correction, not a weakened gate: the assertion
        still creates a real directory whose name is not ASCII, runs a real
        process from it, and checks the result.  What changed is that the JVM can
        now spell the name.

        A PRODUCT-LEVEL CONSEQUENCE FOR A LATER PHASE, recorded here because this
        is where it was found: CometGUI installed on a host whose locale is POSIX
        would be unable to open a spectrum file whose name is not ASCII, for the
        same reason and through no fault of its own.  Phase 16 owns the packaged
        runtime's environment.
      -->
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
        <configuration>
          <environmentVariables>
            <LANG>C.UTF-8</LANG>
            <LC_ALL>C.UTF-8</LC_ALL>
          </environmentVariables>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
